From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:12:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve with nab-resolver behind --use-feature=nab-resolver

nab-resolver, vendored beside resolvelib, is a PubGrub solver. With
--use-feature=nab-resolver it searches for the answer in place of
resolvelib; everything around the search -- pip's factory, candidates,
requirements, provider, the RequirementSet it builds and the errors it
reports -- is pip's, as with resolvelib. Each of pip's requirements is the
range of the versions its finder offers for it, versions are chosen in
pip's order (a direct requirement's own candidate, an installed version
kept, then newest first) and built only when chosen, and a failure is
reported through the requirements nab's derivation names, in pip's words.
